Check file upload → validate PDF/TXT → ensure not blank → extract content → verify data exists → generate answer → cache result for faster future access.


1- Check if a file is uploaded or exists; if not, return “Please upload a file first before clicking Load”

2- Validate the file type to ensure only PDF or TXT files are accepted; otherwise return “Unsupported file type”

3- Check whether the file is blank by verifying size or content; if it is empty, return “PDF has no readable text (blank or scanned PDF)” or "Uploaded file is empty"

4- Extract the content from the file after all validations are successfully passed.

5- Verify whether the required data exists in the extracted content; if not found, return “Data not found in document”

6- Process both dropdown sample questions and custom user questions using the same logic flow.

7- Generate the answer based on the extracted and validated file content.

8- Store the first successful result in cache memory to improve performance and return cached results for repeated requests with the same input.
